    ],
    "apps" : {
        "172.17.0.1:3000" : {
            "name": "juice shop",
            "version": "1.2.3",
            "vulns": [
                {"id":"GHSA-vf2r-cxg9-p7rf", "notes": "...", "applies": "not-checked"}
            ]
        },
        "172.17.0.1:8080": {
            "name": "wordpress",
            "version": "2.1.0",
            "vulns": [
                {"id":"RLSA-2025:7432", "notes": "...", "applies": "yes"}
            ]
        }
    }
}

# You follow this specific process:
1. pick server to check and put into .servers
2. find open ports for the servers and put into .ports
3. find which apps are running on these ports and their versions and put into .apps
5. use curl and a osv.dev website to check for platform or apps vulnerabilities and put into .vulns
6. check if this vulnerabillity applies and active

Repeat until you've finished the scanning process.
Be concise, I just need a final report
